WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.250
In Hollywood, it usually takes a little while
for a new box office record-breaker to emerge,

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.460
but it does happen eventually.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.520
Right now, Avengers: Endgame holds the crown…but
for how long?

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.840
Here's a look at some of the upcoming movies
that might just be able to cut short Endgame's

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:14.380
all-time reign.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.380
It's pretty much a certainty that Star Wars:
The Rise of Skywalker will be one of the year's

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.390
biggest releases.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.630
While Star Wars is one of the highest-grossing
franchises in American history, only A New

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.010
Hope ever reached the top spot to become the
highest grossing movie worldwide.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:33.340
A lot has happened since 1977, with international
grosses playing a much bigger role in a film's

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:33.940
performance.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.540
And while Star Wars certainly is as ubiquitous
as ever, the two most recent films in the

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.170
series didn't quite hit Endgame levels at
either the domestic or international box office.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.470
The spinoff Solo: A Star Wars Story underwhelmed
financially, while 2017's The Last Jedi made

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:54.200
$620 million domestically and $1.3 billion
worldwide, which is pretty damned impressive

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.180
to be sure, but it's still less than its predecessor
The Force Awakens, and far less than Endgame.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.040
Throughout the nine-film, three-trilogy Skywalker
Saga, a pattern has tended to emerge: in which

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:08.760
the second film in each trilogy dips domestically
before the final installment dominates the

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:09.759
box office.

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:13.390
However, to top the numbers worldwide, you
need a strong international showing, and Star

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:16.920
Wars' foreign totals typically just aren't
as great as the MCU's.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.081
For example, while The Force Awakens is the
highest-grossing domestic release ever, it's

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.579
only fourth worldwide.

00:01:22.579 --> 00:01:26.640
So while The Rise of Skywalker may very well
top Avengers: Endgame at the domestic box

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.360
office, it looks like a long shot to set the
worldwide record.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.540
The Jurassic Park franchise has always been
a stalwart showing at the box office, so what

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.360
are Jurassic World 3's chances of topping
Endgame when it opens in June 2021?

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.020
Well, Jurassic Park was the highest-grossing
film ever worldwide until Titanic took the

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.020
top spot.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.070
And while the later instalments in the first
trilogy opened to more tepid reactions, Jurassic

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:53.689
World set a record for opening weekend and
enjoyed a stunning final gross of $652 million

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:57.469
domestic and almost $1.7 billion worldwide.

00:01:57.469 --> 00:02:00.020
"Life, uh, finds a way."

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.960
Its sequel, Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom,
didn't do quite as well, however, although

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.820
it's probably fair to say Universal isn't
crying about its $1.3 billion global take.

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.780
All in all, the Jurassic franchise seems to
be following an all-too-familiar pattern.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:17.760
Audiences flock to the first one, but once
the novelty has worn off, the grosses get

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.040
smaller and smaller.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.790
Don't expect to see the Jurassic series go
extinct anytime soon, but don't expect it

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.900
to gobble up Earth's Mightiest Heroes, either.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.320
Avengers 5 doesn't have a title, a storyline,
or even a release date.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.900
Heck, it's not even a part of Marvel's Phase
4, as far as anyone knows.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.069
And yet it's one of the most anticipated movies
in the near future, if for no other reason

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:39.739
than it follows the record-smashing Avengers:
Endgame.

00:02:39.739 --> 00:02:43.959
Whatever form Avengers 5 takes, a few things
are certain: namely that some of Endgame's

00:02:43.959 --> 00:02:45.939
biggest stars will be nowhere in sight.

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.180
So don't expect Robert Downey Jr., Chris Evans,
Scarlett Johansson, or Josh Brolin to show

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:50.760
up.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.820
The real question is, then, whether Avengers
5 will have the same draw without these cornerstone

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:55.800
characters?

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.020
Of course, it's possible.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:01.570
Black Panther, Captain Marvel, and Spider-Man
have each made bank at the box office, and

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.790
you know the studio will pull no punches in
making Avengers 5 just as big an event as

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.969
its predecessor.

00:03:06.969 --> 00:03:10.709
But whether it's enough, and whether Marvel's
lightning can strike twice, well, that remains

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:11.260
to be seen.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.320
Of course, it's entirely possible that it
won't take every Avenger to top Endgame's

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:15.860
gross.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.880
Maybe it'll only take one, Black Panther.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:22.870
Thanks to its insane $700 million domestic
gross, Black Panther is the highest-grossing

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:27.230
solo superhero movie, with a take-in of $1.3
billion worldwide.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:30.540
That's bigger than anything put out by any
other superhero, ever.

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.720
Clearly Black Panther scratched an itch.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.400
So what does that mean for a sequel?

00:03:34.409 --> 00:03:38.799
With the notable exceptions of Iron Man 2
and Avengers: Age of Ultron, just about every

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:42.920
MCU sequel has made more than the previous
film, both domestically and worldwide.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.770
That means the sky seems to be the limit for
the King of Wakanda's future adventures, but

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.670
the question is, just how high can he go?

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.530
Can Black Panther's historic gross be bettered
with its sequel?

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.400
Or was the record-breaking gross of Black
Panther the consequence of a perfect storm

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.930
of culture and cross-promotion colliding?

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:02.379
Much like Avengers 5, the title, storyline
and complete cast for this sequel are still

00:04:02.379 --> 00:04:06.810
unknown, and all anyone knows is that it's
due for release on May 6th 2022.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:11.420
But what we do know is that, while Black Panther's
domestic take was historic, its overseas grosses

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:13.530
were a little lower than other Marvel movies.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.630
To really outdo Endgame, Black Panther II
is going to have to up its international game

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.200
considerably.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:23.240
If any single superhero can take down Earth's
Mightiest Heroes, it's gonna be Batman.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.400
Arguably the most popular costumed vigilante
on the big screen, Batman's combined domestic

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.169
gross is $2.4 billion.

00:04:29.169 --> 00:04:33.259
If we adjust that for inflation, given most
Batman movies came out more than 10 years

00:04:33.259 --> 00:04:35.620
ago, it's $3.5 billion.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.490
This is also the only franchise to break the
opening weekend record four times, although

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:43.220
no Batman movie has been the highest-grossing
film ever, domestically or worldwide.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.220
"All you care about is money.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:48.520
This town deserves a better class of criminal.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.600
And I'm gonna give it to them."

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:56.980
The biggest hit in the franchise, The Dark
Knight, made $533 million domestically, placing

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.340
it second behind Titanic in North America.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:04.800
The Dark Knight's worldwide take, however,
barely makes the top 50 at just over $1 billion.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.770
Ever since The Dark Knight Rises, Batman has
kind of been in a dry spell, but The Batman

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:12.270
hopes to change that when it opens on June
25th 2021.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:16.800
The movie's connection to the DCEU is unclear,
but it promises to be a complete reboot for

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:21.080
the character, and the last reboot in the
series, Batman Begins, performed well, setting

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:23.449
the stage for the record-breaking Dark Knight.

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:27.500
And sure, there's been a little fan backlash
after Robert Pattinson's casting in the title

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.660
role, but fans protested Michael Keaton's
casting, too.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.210
Shows what they know.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:37.120
Indiana Jones 5, scheduled for a July 9th
2021 release, is shrouded in more secrecy

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.050
than the Ark of the Covenant itself.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.530
But what can we expect from its box office
performance?

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:44.979
Indiana Jones' total domestic gross is just
over $906 million.

00:05:44.979 --> 00:05:50.259
And while that might seem unimpressive, adjusted
for inflation, that comes to $2.1 billion

00:05:50.259 --> 00:05:54.250
domestically across just four films, which
is pretty incredible.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:58.220
Still, it's hard to gauge how Indy will do
in a new environment driven by international

00:05:58.220 --> 00:05:59.220
grosses.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:05.240
Indiana Jones and The Kingdom of the Crystal
Skull made $317 million stateside and $786

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.640
million worldwide in 2008.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:12.300
Not great, but not bad, although as we saw
with Star Wars: The Force Awaken's historic

00:06:12.319 --> 00:06:16.509
run, fans really, really like seeing Harrison
Ford playing his most iconic characters.

00:06:16.509 --> 00:06:17.940
"It's not the years, hon.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:20.120
It's the mileage."

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.710
And while Indy has never been quite at the
level of Lucasfilm's golden goose from the

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:29.040
galaxy far, far away, it's still a franchise
that enjoys a rock solid place in pop culture

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:29.760
history.

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:33.940
Indy 5 might not be a front-runner for becoming
the highest-grossing movie of all time, but

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.820
it might just become the highest-grossing
Indy film worldwide, and could well make enough

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:40.360
money for Disney to fill up a whole Temple
of Doom.

00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:45.880
The Skywalker Saga isn't the only Star Wars-related
media Disney has slated for release over the

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.520
next few years, far from it.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:52.200
Currently, Game of Thrones showrunners David
Benioff and D.B. Weiss are working on a Star

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:56.419
Wars trilogy, while The Last Jedi director
Rian Johnson is working on his own, too.

00:06:56.419 --> 00:07:00.159
On top of that, Marvel head honcho Kevin Feige
is developing a film for the studio.

00:07:00.159 --> 00:07:04.520
All in all, the studio has Star Wars films
booked through the next decade, trading holiday

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:09.110
release dates with Avatar sequels in a bid
to dominate the universe, one December at

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:09.600
a time.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:13.520
It's doubtful that Disney needs or even cares
if any of these films break away to become

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:14.810
the biggest of all time.

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.210
Sure, they wouldn't complain if any of them
did, but that's not exactly the goal.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:22.169
The real goal, however, is to replicate the
MCU's multi-franchise formula.

00:07:22.169 --> 00:07:25.940
And while that sounds good in theory, Solo
proved that you can't make bank just by slapping

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:27.430
the Star Wars name on it.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:31.199
Still, with a slew of talent behind these
upcoming movies, plus the influence of the

00:07:31.199 --> 00:07:35.430
man who made Marvel what it is today, LucasFilm
could find themselves raking in the credits

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.460
very, very soon.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:41.940
James Cameron has been teasing the expansion
of his Avatar franchise for so long that most

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:44.270
fans have gone Na'vi blue in the face by now.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:48.470
Cameras have finally started rolling on no
fewer than four Avatar sequels, at a total

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:49.909
cost of $1 billion.

00:07:49.909 --> 00:07:54.210
That may seem like a crazy investment on a
franchise that'll be 12 years old by the time

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:59.570
the next one arrives in 2021, but this is
Avatar, after all: until July 2019, it was

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:03.729
the highest-grossing film ever worldwide,
and it remains the highest-grossing overseas.

00:08:03.729 --> 00:08:08.020
Heck, the first Avatar sequel could bomb and
the franchise would still be one of the biggest

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.610
ever based on the first film's performance
alone.

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:11.960
But that's unlikely to happen.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:16.350
The past decade has seen many pundits predicting
Cameron's Avatar sequels will fail, mostly

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:20.190
stemming from the fact that Avatar doesn't
have the same hold on pop culture as say,

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:21.190
Star Wars or Lord of the Rings.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:25.909
And that may be so, but once that first trailer
hits, finally showcasing whatever CG-induced

00:08:25.909 --> 00:08:30.099
fever dream Cameron has cooked up, you can
bet your bottom dollar that fans will be pre-ordering

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:31.380
their tickets in their droves.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:33.980
But hey, why start from scratch?

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:38.520
Who says an Avatar sequel has to top Avengers:
Endgame when Avatar already has a head start?

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:43.180
Less than $10 million separates Avatar and
Endgame, so if Avatar were to be re-released

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:47.160
to build anticipation for its sequels, there's
a solid chance it would take its record back.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:51.300
Rereleasing films is nothing new, though it
hasn't been as common a thing since the arrival

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.200
of home entertainment and on-demand streaming
services.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.240
But what's a little friendly competition when
a world record is at stake?

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:01.860
The only problem is, since Disney purchased
Fox, Disney would be responsible for the reissue,

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.890
meaning they'd be competing with themselves.

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:07.420
Disney obviously wanted Endgame to take the
record, hence the decision to re-release the

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:10.990
movie a few months after release with just
a few minutes of extra footage.

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:14.510
Now that they've done it, why would they turn
around and have Avatar usurp it?

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.390
Money matters, but pride counts too.

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:20.900
Now that Disney owns Fox, expect Avatar to
stay right where it is: firmly behind Avengers:

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:21.560
Endgame.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:25.480
Nobody would have predicted James Cameron's
movie about the sinking of a big boat would

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:27.640
become the highest-grossing movie ever.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:32.250
Even fewer predicted that Cameron would top
his own record with an original sci-fi film

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.950
about space marines fighting 12-foot blue
aliens.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:38.950
Yes, everybody knew Endgame was going to own
the box office, but nobody predicted that

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:43.290
C-List superhero Iron Man would spawn history's
most successful franchise, either.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.070
So who knows what could happen in the future?

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:49.300
Despite the endless data and analytics that
go into every Hollywood movie, which movies

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:52.600
hit big and which films flop hard really is
anyone's guess.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:57.279
Hollywood is knee-deep in the IP era, but
as summer 2019 has proven, lots of moviegoers

00:09:57.279 --> 00:09:59.290
are suffering from sequelitis.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:02.820
Maybe the future highest-grossing film won't
be a franchise entry at all, but an original

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:03.380
work?

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:07.820
Or maybe it'll be based on a popular book,
or maybe, like Titanic, Gone with the Wind,

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:12.860
and so many huge box office hits before, it'll
be some kind of epic historical romance.

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:15.050
Maybe the biggest hit won't even come from
America.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:20.089
With a gross of more than $700 million, 2019's
seventh highest-grossing movie worldwide is

00:10:20.089 --> 00:10:21.950
the Chinese film The Wandering Earth.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.720
Could a foreign film become a breakout hit
it in the U.S.?

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.720
As with all things, only time will tell.

